[{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-869"
  :itonami.blueprint/name "Other Human Health Activities - Non-Emergency Transport Coordination"
  :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev4 "869"
  :itonami.blueprint/domain :services/health-support-coordination
  :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
  :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:operational-efficiency :accessibility :patient-transport-coordination :vehicle-management]
  :itonami.blueprint/governor :transport-governor
  :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
  :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger]
  :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
  :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
  :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
  "TransportAdvisor ⊣ TransportGovernor, langgraph-clj StateGraph
  (langgraph.graph, transportops.operation/build), append-only audit
  ledger (transportops.store/ledger + append-ledger!, MemStore). Fixes
  a prior gap: `operation.cljc`'s own docstring claimed \"the
  langgraph-clj StateGraph\" and `deps.edn` declared a real
  `io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph` dependency, but `execute-proposal`
  was actually a plain `(-> state intake-node advise-node govern-node
  decide-node commit-node)` threading pipeline -- zero `require` of
  `langgraph.graph`, zero use of `state-graph`/`add-node`/
  `compile-graph` anywhere in the file. Now: a genuinely compiled
  StateGraph (`:intake -> :advise -> :govern -> :decide -+->
  :commit / :request-approval -> :commit / :hold`) with
  `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` + in-memory checkpointer for
  real human-in-the-loop resume. The Governor (three HARD, permanent,
  un-overridable checks: vehicle-unverified, effect-not-propose,
  scope-excluded emergency/clinical content) and the append-only audit
  ledger were already genuinely wired in the pre-graph pipeline
  (`store/append-ledger!` was real, not dead code) -- both are
  preserved unchanged, and the ledger wiring now also durably records
  every `:hold` (governor violation or phase-ineligible), not only
  auto-commits. Five closed-allowlist ops
  (`:schedule-transport` / `:coordinate-vehicle-availability` /
  `:coordinate-supply-request` / `:schedule-staff-shift-proposal` /
  `:flag-safety-concern`), all `:effect :propose` only.
  `:flag-safety-concern` ALWAYS escalates to a human dispatcher via the
  compiled graph's `:request-approval` node
  (`interrupt-before`, checkpoint-based resume, proven by
  `test/transportops/operation_test.clj` exercising commit /
  hard-hold (unregistered + unverified vehicle) / phase-hold /
  escalate-approve / escalate-reject through the REAL compiled graph
  end to end, plus a `clojure -M:dev:run` demo runner producing real
  ledger entries for every scenario). 27 tests / 133 assertions green
  (`clojure -M:dev:test`), clj-kondo 0 errors, demo runnable
  end-to-end. Governance-doc set (LICENSE, GOVERNANCE.md,
  CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md), `docs/` (business
  model + operator guide), and CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`,
  sibling-checkout pattern for `:local/root` deps) added -- this repo
  previously had none of those, unique among its cloud-itonami-isic-*
  siblings."
  :db/id -1}]
